# Small-system (8 atoms) LAMMPS ground truth for cross-validating exaStamp's new
# compute_descriptor_snap_global against real LAMMPS compute snap. Like compute pod/global,
# this produces a GLOBAL ARRAY (not per-atom), exported via immediate-variable c_ID[i][j]
# syntax since ordinary dump cannot export it. Rows/cols (31 x 31) are specific to this fixed
# 8-atom Ta_small system + param.txt (ncoeff=30, ntypes=1 -> 31 cols; 1+3*8+6=31 rows).
# Column 31 (the last) is LAMMPS's own reference-energy/force/virial label column -- exaStamp's
# compute_descriptor_snap_global deliberately has no such column, so compare_global.py drops it.

